From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:29:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Guard: nothing pushes the client; log the last attack

The push allowance was wrong: EntityLivingBase.onLivingUpdate runs
collideWithNearbyEntities only when !world.isRemote, in 1.8 as in 1.7, and
the server never sends a player its own push. Players do not push each other
on the client, so the 0.0708 per overlapping entity was only a gap for a
speed cheat standing next to someone. Removed.

Both speed flags seen so far came from the attacking player; a failed move
check now also says how many ticks ago it last attacked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaGuard.java
